        <start_date>2004-01-04</start_date>
        <stop_date>2018-06-10</stop_date>
        <description>
            MERIGOLD (Mars Exploration Rover In-Situ Global Observations Localization Dataset)
            is a derived data archive that gives Mars global map coordinates for the science
            observations made by the Mars Exploration Rovers Spirit and Opportunity during their
            missions. MERIGOLD provides one localization record for each input science data product.
            Each record gives the observation location in a common global coordinate system,
            together with the rover state and instrument geometry used to compute it. With these
            records, users can find where an observation was made, which other instruments observed
            the same place, and how observations from different rover positions relate, without
            needing rover operations experience or understanding. MERIGOLD was funded by the
            NASA ROSES 2020 Planetary Data Archiving, Restoration, and Tools (PDART) program.
        </description>
    </Investigation>
